_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-06-13T16:25:14Z","updated_at":"2017-06-13T16:25:14Z","body":"But where do you get those values from, and how are they verified? If you go digging into some proprietary source code, find the channel count and use that magic number, there's no way to know if that applies to a single version of the decoder/software, or if that value is later changed, or even if another EAC3 decoder uses the same value.\r\n\r\nTo me, the 2 solutions are: \r\n1. the original behavior -- ask the android system for the channel count (which returns the wrong value in this case); \r\n2. Fall back to the spec. Because the decoder should follow the spec.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/308172286/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"cspencer404","id":20114776,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMTE0Nzc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20114776?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cspencer404","html_url":"https://github.com/cspencer404","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cspencer404/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cspencer404/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cspencer404/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cspencer404/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cspencer404/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cspencer404/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cspencer404/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cspencer404/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cspencer404/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/Exo